{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1487233-homebrew-suggestions","id":1487233,"title":"Homebrew suggestions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T12:48:14-07:00","id":1487233,"title":"Homebrew suggestions?","content":"Ok, I\u2019m wanting to do some homebrew, but right now I want to focus on two games\u2014-Deviant and Mummy. Each gameline would have me designing a setting, but it would have to focus exclusively on either DtR or MtC. Each book would focus on one gameline, and I\u2019d flesh it out as far as I could.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to use real cities and/or regions. I want imaginative pairings of locations/cultures/mythologies combined with one of the two above-mentioned splats, but I want to take something dissonant to what most people picture those game lines involving. Say, a Deviant setting involving Athabaskan mythology, or Mummy involving Cape Canaveral and NASA. A combination of setting and gameline that wouldn\u2019t occur to most.<br /> <br /> Plus, I\u2019ve already decided to try my hand at some small-scale homebrewing, which leads me to do a Writeup of Gobkle Tempi. I\u2019ll post it as soon as I\u2019ve something to post.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T16:51:06-07:00","id":1487276,"title":"","content":"So a few questions come to mind:<br /> <br /> 1. What sort of scope in setting are you looking for? Mummies divide their territories into &quot;Nomes&quot; and assign 7 to 10 'nomarchs' to oversee immortal concerns within that region (conceivably could be a large territory but generally assumed to be a city). But the game could focus on a single cult run by one Arisen with the players playing mortals or lesser immortal followers of the Deathless. Are you looking for a relatively populous setting full of several Arisen working and competing with each other? Are you looking for a smaller setting, perhaps involving a single group of mummies (or a meret, as the game calls it)? Something smaller still, like a singular isolated court? Such things will have a significant impact on the setting.<br /> <br /> 2. How extensive a write up are you looking for? A brief paragraph? Pages of info, similar to the cities described under Mummy second edition?<br /> <br /> 3. Do you want specific examples or a broader discussion on setting building? And what are you planning to do with the material? Do you just want ideas, or are you publishing some fan supplement? How many details would you like filled in and how much do you want to fill in yourself? <br /> <br /> I keep meaning to write up a blurb for my setting in Saint Louis, Missouri. And I keep overthinking it and turning it into too big a project. This would be a good excuse to try again.<br /> <br /> (Just a heads up, I personally am only going to discuss Mummy the Curse, and I am an old grognar that knows First Edition way better than Second. No offense to Deviant, I'm sure it is an excellent game. The idea just never sparked much interest from me and I have no plans to pick up the book- I like the general idea of something akin to Island of Dr. Moureau meets the Hills have Eyes, it just doesn't interest me as an entire game line unto itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T19:12:59-07:00","id":1487300,"title":"","content":"1)A full setting, ie, a city or location of great import. Gobekli Tepi is one such example I\u2019ve already settled on. As to the Arisen population, I\u2019ll scale it as seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> 2)Pages of info.<br /> <br /> 3)Spevific examples. Not publishing, but for an upcoming campaign. I\u2019ll post it all here though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T18:26:11-08:00","id":1497596,"title":"","content":"Well, Kamakhya, India is my choice for Mummy. Even if my PbP fails to materialize, I\u2019ve learned enough about the temple-complex to inspire me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T22:57:01-08:00","id":1497775,"title":"","content":"Whats going on in Egypt? How many Deviants, in addition to the random Prometheans and Bound, have been made by people trying to make immortals? It isnt even that HARD to make BETTER immortal deviants (Anomalous Biology 5, Rapid Healing 5). The Sphinx and the Shuanksen are surely not the only reasons Mummies had their Diaspora.. <br /> <br /> But to flip the script as you want to, youd have to take the games and flip them. Ie the Arisen are the broken souls with no meaning, trying to fight their conspiratorial guilds.. while the deviant version shows the deviants as the true ancient blessed immortal heroes, their &quot;broken&quot; souls purified and literally balanced on the scales of ma'at (endgame is getting Conviction AND Loyalty to 3 each somehow) i guess it still has the crossover if you use both, but if you used deviant in egypt ot would be out of place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}